.TH EUCLID-CLI-ESM-DELETE-OBJECT 1 "August 2026" "euclid-cli 1.0.53" "Euclid CLI Manual"
.SH NAME
euclid-cli-esm-delete-object \- delete a storage object
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B euclid-cli esm delete-object
.BR \-\-ern | \-e
.I ERN
[\fB\-\-version\-id\fR|\fB\-V\fR \fIID\fR]
.SH DESCRIPTION
Deletes a storage object identified by its Euclid resource name (ERN).
In a bucket with versioning, every version kept of the object goes with
it, files included. This cannot be undone.
.PP
With
.BR \-\-version\-id ,
only that version is deleted. A non-current version is simply removed,
and the object reads as before. Deleting the current version makes the
newest remaining version the current object again, so the key answers
with the last thing stored in it before the deleted version; the answer
names it as
.IR currentVersionId .
Deleting the only version deletes the object.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.BR \-e ", " \-\-ern " " \fIERN\fR
Euclid resource name of the object to delete. Required.
.TP
.BR \-V ", " \-\-version\-id " " \fIID\fR
Delete only this version; see
.BR euclid-cli-esm-list-object-versions (1).
.SH EXIT STATUS
.TP
.B 0
The object was deleted. No output is printed.
.TP
.B 1
Missing/invalid arguments, the server could not be reached, or no
object with that ERN exists.
.SH EXAMPLES
.RS
.nf
euclid-cli --endpoint http://localhost:5566 esm delete-object \e
    --ern ern:esm:eu-central-1:000000000000:development:object:reports/2026-08.csv
.fi
.RE
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR euclid-cli-esm (1),
.BR euclid-cli-esm-upload-file (1),
.BR euclid-cli-esm-list-objects (1)
